.TH tudate n 0.3 tclutils
.SH tclutils::tudate
.PP
Flexible date helpers built on the Tcl \fBclock\fR command: parse common formats, render ISO, do calendar arithmetic, day differences and human relative phrases. Works in local time.
.SS API
.CS
set t [::tclutils::tudate::parse "15.03.2024"]    ;# epoch seconds
::tclutils::tudate::iso $t                         ;# 2024-03-15
.CE
.PP
Commands:
.IP \(bu
\fBparse str ?\-format fmt?\fR — epoch seconds. Without \fB\-format\fR, common formats are tried in this order: ISO date and date\-time (also without seconds and as \fBYYYYMMDD\fR), \fBd.m.Y\fR (with optional time), \fBd/m/Y\fR, \fBY/m/d\fR, \fBm/d/Y\fR, \fBH:M:S\fR, \fBH:M\fR, \fBd Mon Y\fR, \fBMon d Y\fR, \fBMon d, Y\fR (English month names). \fB02/03/2026\fR is 2 March; \fBm/d/Y\fR only applies when \fBd/m/Y\fR gives no date, so \fB10/29/2026\fR is 29 October. Then a free\-form \fBclock scan\fR, but not for a string of digits and separators only. Errors \fB{TCLUTILS TUDATE PARSE}\fR.
.IP \(bu
A day or month that does not exist is an error, with or without \fB\-format\fR, on Tcl 8.6 and 9.0 alike: \fB2026\-02\-29\fR, \fB31.04.2026\fR, \fB29/02/2026\fR, \fBFeb 30 2026\fR. Tcl 8.6's \fBclock scan\fR alone would roll these over (\fB2026\-03\-01\fR, \fB2026\-05\-01\fR, \fB2028\-05\-02\fR); \fBparse\fR formats each match back and rejects it when the numbers differ (0.3).
.IP \(bu
\fBiso seconds ?\-time bool?\fR — \fByyyy\-mm\-dd\fR (or \fB...THH:MM:SS\fR).
.IP \(bu
\fBadd seconds count unit\fR — calendar add; unit second/minute/hour/day/week/ month/year (plural or singular). Errors \fB{TCLUTILS TUDATE UNIT}\fR.
.IP \(bu
\fBdiff a b ?\-unit days?\fR — integer difference (seconds/minutes/hours/days/weeks).
.IP \(bu
\fBrelative seconds ?\-base secs?\fR — "today", "yesterday", "in N days", etc.
.IP \(bu
\fBtoday\fR — today's ISO date.
.IP \(bu
\fBzones\fR — sorted time zone names for \fBclock format \-timezone\fR (e.g. \fBEurope/Berlin\fR), from Tcl's tzdata, else the system zoneinfo; always includes \fBUTC\fR. Names from the system directory are checked with \fBclock\fR first (Tcl 8.6 without own tzdata rejects \fBEtc/GMT+1\fR etc.) (0.2).
